  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nWhile upstreaming the Sanitizer API https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#canonicalize-the-configuration got rewritten to:\n\n1. [For each](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-iterate) member of configuration that is a list of strings:\n    1. Replace each string in member with the result of [canonicalizing](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#canonicalize-a-sanitizer-name) it.\n\nLooking at this now, it feels too loosely defined. I made two observations:\n- Not every member has a canonicalization (comments, dataAttributes)\n- The link for _canonicalizing_ points to https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#canonicalize-a-sanitizer-name, which isn't correct for e.g. PIs.\n\nWas there a strong reason to go with this approach instead of the more explicit steps in the WICG draft?\n\n@noamr @annevk ",
